From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Druchenko <bananos@dev.co.ua>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:23:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] b43: N-PHY: rev 13 upper gain update RF sequence as wl

wl 5.110 programs RF sequence command 5 (update gain U: RX gain, clear
HIQ disable, HPF bandwidth) on radio 2057 rev 13 with delays 6, 15, 1;
b43 did so only on revs 1-2. Do it in the rev 13 2.4 GHz gain control
setup.

On an ASUS RT-N12 D1 the microcode's bad FCS and bad PLCP counters over
a throughput run roughly halved (6290 / 2710 to 3048 / 1565); throughput
is unchanged (AP->client 12.9 Mbit/s, client->AP 20.6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
index 7854186..9fe2acb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -2563,6 +2563,16 @@ static void b43_nphy_gain_ctl_workarounds_2057_rev13_2g(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 	b43_phy_write(dev, B43_PHY_N(0x169), 0x1c02);
 	b43_phy_write(dev, B43_PHY_N(0x300), 0x0155);
 	b43_phy_write(dev, B43_PHY_N(0x301), 0x0155);
+
+	/* The RF sequence of an upper gain update (RX gain, clear HIQ
+	 * disable, HPF bandwidth), with wl's delays */
+	{
+		u8 events[] = { 0x7, 0x8, 0xe };
+		u8 delays[] = { 0x6, 0xf, 0x1 };
+
+		b43_nphy_set_rf_sequence(dev, B43_RFSEQ_UPDATE_GAINU, events,
+					 delays, ARRAY_SIZE(events));
+	}
 }
 
 static void b43_nphy_gain_ctl_workarounds_rev7(struct b43_wldev *dev)
